Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-04-24
Subject: Fix csopt386 CheckSequence FillWord count: words not bytes
License: expat

`compiler/i386/csopt386.pas` initialises the `new2oldreg` map with

  fillword(new2oldreg, sizeof(new2oldreg), RS_INVALID);

`FillWord`'s second argument is the number of 16-bit words to write,
but `sizeof(new2oldreg)` is the size in BYTES. The call therefore
writes twice as many words as the array holds and scribbles past the
end of `new2oldreg` into whatever follows it in the stack frame.

Divide by `sizeof(word)` so the count is in words, matching what
`FillWord` actually wants.

This is a real upstream FPC bug!

diff --git a/compiler/i386/csopt386.pas b/compiler/i386/csopt386.pas
--- a/compiler/i386/csopt386.pas
+++ b/compiler/i386/csopt386.pas
@@ -427,7 +427,7 @@ begin {CheckSequence}
   with startRegInfo do
     begin
       newRegsEncountered := [RS_EBP, RS_ESP];
-      fillword(new2oldreg,sizeof(new2oldreg),RS_INVALID);
+      fillword(new2oldreg,sizeof(new2oldreg) div sizeof(word),RS_INVALID);
       new2OldReg[RS_EBP] := RS_EBP;
       new2OldReg[RS_ESP] := RS_ESP;
       oldRegsEncountered := newRegsEncountered;
